@2.2.1/2 | T | Backslash-newline is a line continuation, removed before tokens are split, and is not a token separator
> quote/continuation
--- quote/c_continuation_joins
ec\
ho a\
b
x=1\
2; echo $x
@2.2.2/1 | T | Single quotes preserve the literal value of every character within them
> quote/single
--- quote/c_single_all
echo '$HOME `date` \n "dq" * ? [a] ~ #no'
echo 'a
b'
@2.2.3/1 | T | Within double quotes $ keeps its meaning for parameter, command and arithmetic expansion
> quote/double
--- quote/c_dq_dollar
