--- quote/c_ds_octal oracle=bash
printf '%s' $'\101\1012\7x' | od -An -tx1 | tr -d '[:space:]'; echo
@2.2.4/6 | T | An escaped single quote does not end a $'...' sequence, and the sequence joins with adjacent word parts
--- quote/c_ds_embedded oracle=bash
x=$'it\'s'; echo "$x"
echo a$'\t'b"c"$'d'
@2.2.4/7 | T | $'...' escapes are processed before word expansion: the result is quoted (not split, not globbed)
