@2.5.3/16 | T | The shell processes values as characters where the standard speaks of characters (${#x} counts characters)
! the corpus runs in the C locale, where a character is a byte; the UTF-8 answer is measured by hand (docs/CENSUS.md, locale rows)
--- param/c_length_bytes_in_c
x=$(printf '\303\251\303\250')
echo ${#x}
